WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.350 --> 00:00:04.839
Hello, everyone! I'm Ms. Emma. Welcome to Online B one, Book one.

2
00:00:05.139 --> 00:00:08.468
Hi! I'm Visal. Let's learn together!

3
00:00:08.768 --> 00:00:14.555
Unit twenty-two: Cooking at Home. Today you will give instructions for cooking a dish in order.

4
00:00:14.855 --> 00:00:17.565
Here is our lesson map. Let's start!

5
00:00:18.500 --> 00:00:21.802
Part one: words. You will learn eight new words.

6
00:00:22.650 --> 00:00:23.616
Recipe.

7
00:00:24.617 --> 00:00:27.522
Recipe means instructions for making a dish.

8
00:00:28.117 --> 00:00:30.546
This is my grandma's recipe for lok lak.

9
00:00:31.150 --> 00:00:33.918
Your turn. Say: Recipe.

10
00:00:36.767 --> 00:00:37.884
Recipe.

11
00:00:38.650 --> 00:00:39.721
Ingredient.

12
00:00:40.717 --> 00:00:43.541
Ingredient means one of the foods you use in a dish.

13
00:00:44.150 --> 00:00:45.941
Beef is the main ingredient.

14
00:00:46.550 --> 00:00:48.854
Your turn. Say: Ingredient.

15
00:00:51.700 --> 00:00:52.864
Ingredient.

16
00:00:53.617 --> 00:00:54.223
Chop.

17
00:00:55.217 --> 00:00:57.599
Chop means to cut into small pieces.

18
00:00:58.183 --> 00:00:59.626
Chop the garlic finely.

19
00:01:00.217 --> 00:01:02.428
Your turn. Say: Chop.

20
00:01:05.267 --> 00:01:06.036
Chop.

21
00:01:06.783 --> 00:01:07.587
Boil.

22
00:01:08.583 --> 00:01:11.012
Boil means to cook in very hot water.

23
00:01:11.617 --> 00:01:13.651
Boil the noodles for three minutes.

24
00:01:14.250 --> 00:01:16.728
Your turn. Say: Boil.

25
00:01:19.567 --> 00:01:20.382
Boil.

26
00:01:21.117 --> 00:01:21.932
Fry.

27
00:01:22.917 --> 00:01:24.835
Fry means to cook in hot oil.

28
00:01:25.450 --> 00:01:27.101
Fry the egg in a little oil.

29
00:01:27.717 --> 00:01:30.021
Your turn. Say: Fry.

30
00:01:32.867 --> 00:01:33.682
Fry.

31
00:01:34.417 --> 00:01:35.232
Taste.

32
00:01:36.217 --> 00:01:39.261
Taste means to try a little food to check the flavor.

33
00:01:39.850 --> 00:01:41.803
Taste the soup before you serve it.

34
00:01:42.417 --> 00:01:45.533
Your turn. Say: Taste.

35
00:01:48.400 --> 00:01:49.239
Taste.

36
00:01:49.983 --> 00:01:50.787
Meal.

37
00:01:51.783 --> 00:01:54.944
Meal means food you eat at one time, like lunch.

38
00:01:55.550 --> 00:01:57.062
Dinner is our biggest meal.

39
00:01:57.650 --> 00:02:00.221
Your turn. Say: Meal.

40
00:02:03.067 --> 00:02:03.859
Meal.

41
00:02:04.617 --> 00:02:05.397
Kitchen.

42
00:02:06.383 --> 00:02:08.197
Kitchen means the room where you cook.

43
00:02:08.783 --> 00:02:10.411
My mother is in the kitchen.

44
00:02:11.017 --> 00:02:13.321
Your turn. Say: Kitchen.

45
00:02:16.167 --> 00:02:16.959
Kitchen.

46
00:02:17.767 --> 00:02:21.476
Part two: dialogue. Let's listen to a conversation.

47
00:02:22.317 --> 00:02:24.421
Visal, can you cook anything?

48
00:02:25.517 --> 00:02:28.178
Yes, I can make fried rice!

49
00:02:29.283 --> 00:02:30.540
How do you make it?

50
00:02:31.650 --> 00:02:36.590
First, chop the onion and garlic. Then, fry them in oil.

51
00:02:37.683 --> 00:02:38.847
What's next?

52
00:02:39.950 --> 00:02:44.518
After that, add the rice and egg. Finally, taste it and serve!

53
00:02:45.667 --> 00:02:47.631
Part three: grammar.

54
00:02:48.483 --> 00:02:50.680
Grammar focus: Sequencing words.

55
00:02:50.980 --> 00:02:52.260
Look at the pattern.

56
00:02:52.950 --> 00:02:54.311
First, chop the onion.

57
00:02:55.217 --> 00:02:56.427
Then, fry it.

58
00:02:57.317 --> 00:02:59.200
Finally, taste it and serve.

59
00:03:00.167 --> 00:03:04.593
Instructions use the base verb: chop, fry, add, serve.

60
00:03:05.350 --> 00:03:09.805
Be careful! Don't say: First, chop the onion. After, fry it.

61
00:03:11.767 --> 00:03:15.417
Say: First, chop the onion. Then, fry it.

62
00:03:15.717 --> 00:03:18.170
Use 'then' or 'after that' for the next step.

63
00:03:18.967 --> 00:03:21.596
Part four: reading. Read and listen.

64
00:03:22.400 --> 00:03:23.900
Easy Fried Rice.

65
00:03:24.200 --> 00:03:26.270
Cooking at home is healthy and fun.

66
00:03:27.267 --> 00:03:30.172
First, read the recipe and prepare each ingredient.

67
00:03:31.167 --> 00:03:34.339
Then, chop the vegetables and fry them in a hot pan.

68
00:03:35.333 --> 00:03:38.749
After that, add cold rice, an egg and some soy sauce.

69
00:03:39.733 --> 00:03:42.673
Finally, taste the meal before you serve it to your family.

70
00:03:43.767 --> 00:03:47.919
Part five: quiz. Three questions. Are you ready?

71
00:03:48.783 --> 00:03:51.166
First, chop the onion. blank, fry it.

72
00:03:51.466 --> 00:03:54.516
A, Then. B, First. C, Finally.

73
00:03:58.067 --> 00:03:59.602
The answer is A: Then.

74
00:04:00.750 --> 00:04:03.098
Instructions for making a dish are a blank.

75
00:04:03.398 --> 00:04:06.610
A, recipe. B, kitchen. C, meal.

76
00:04:10.167 --> 00:04:12.247
The answer is A: recipe.

77
00:04:13.383 --> 00:04:15.313
To cook in hot oil is to blank.

78
00:04:15.613 --> 00:04:18.872
A, fry. B, boil. C, chop.

79
00:04:22.433 --> 00:04:24.050
The answer is A: fry.

80
00:04:25.233 --> 00:04:28.385
Part six: speaking. It's your turn to talk.

81
00:04:29.250 --> 00:04:30.646
What dish can you cook?

82
00:04:39.450 --> 00:04:40.962
Now listen to Visal.

83
00:04:41.262 --> 00:04:51.094
I can cook fried eggs. First, I heat some oil. Then, I fry the eggs. Finally, I add a little salt and serve them with rice.

84
00:04:51.394 --> 00:04:53.382
Excellent answer, Visal!

85
00:04:54.283 --> 00:04:58.248
Great work! Now you can use eight new words and sequencing words.

86
00:04:58.548 --> 00:05:03.626
Today's value is independence. Learn to do things by yourself, step by step.

87
00:05:03.926 --> 00:05:07.566
See you in Unit twenty-three. Goodbye!

88
00:05:07.866 --> 00:05:10.297
Thank you, Ms. Emma! Bye, everyone!

